1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:03,504
Good morning.

2
00:00:05,840 --> 00:00:07,925
He just looks like an abuser now.

3
00:00:08,008 --> 00:00:08,884
For real.

4
00:00:08,968 --> 00:00:10,553
He's even walking like one.

5
00:00:10,636 --> 00:00:11,637
The filter's on.

6
00:00:17,685 --> 00:00:18,853
Hot, hot.

7
00:00:20,438 --> 00:00:22,773
We're going on a date today.

8
00:00:22,857 --> 00:00:24,024
For real?

9
00:00:24,108 --> 00:00:26,026
Who is he going with?

10
00:00:26,110 --> 00:00:27,403
-Who?
-Misato?

11
00:00:27,486 --> 00:00:28,738
What kind?

12
00:00:29,029 --> 00:00:30,448
It's Misato.

13
00:00:31,198 --> 00:00:32,366
Bonfire.

14
00:00:33,325 --> 00:00:34,493
Camping.

15
00:00:34,577 --> 00:00:35,828
Camping?

16
00:00:36,787 --> 00:00:38,998
And

17
00:00:39,081 --> 00:00:40,958
you'll be getting

18
00:00:41,625 --> 00:00:43,753
talk-mode Ryo-chan.

19
00:00:43,836 --> 00:00:44,962
Are you serious?

20
00:00:45,045 --> 00:00:46,005
And a campfire.

21
00:00:46,088 --> 00:00:46,922
Something quiet.

22
00:00:47,006 --> 00:00:48,174
Well, it's a campfire.

23
00:00:49,258 --> 00:00:50,176
That's the deal.

24
00:00:50,259 --> 00:00:51,343
Thank you.

25
00:00:53,095 --> 00:00:57,016
When she's telling me
all this important information,

26
00:00:58,392 --> 00:01:02,021
I can't just be talking
about superficial stuff.

27
00:01:02,354 --> 00:01:04,356
I can't be closing my eyes.

28
00:01:04,440 --> 00:01:06,609
It's like, what did I come here for?

29
00:01:06,942 --> 00:01:11,322
I need to face her without running away.

30
00:01:11,572 --> 00:01:13,240
Or else it would be rude.

31
00:01:14,950 --> 00:01:19,163
And I'm the type of person
who's run from that all my life.

32
00:01:19,288 --> 00:01:22,124
It might be better if she just

33
00:01:23,125 --> 00:01:25,169
slapped me across the face once.

34
00:01:26,003 --> 00:01:28,506
I want to see what they're like
when they're alone.

35
00:01:28,589 --> 00:01:29,465
Yeah.

36
00:01:29,548 --> 00:01:30,966
Maybe it will be different.

37
00:01:34,553 --> 00:01:35,846
How's it going?

38
00:01:36,764 --> 00:01:38,015
Are you in love?

39
00:01:38,098 --> 00:01:39,767
Am I in love?

40
00:01:40,643 --> 00:01:43,062
I'm not sure.

41
00:01:44,355 --> 00:01:47,566
It's been over a week at this point.

42
00:01:47,650 --> 00:01:49,568
It's going by fast, isn't it?

43
00:01:50,277 --> 00:01:51,695
Time flies.

44
00:01:53,614 --> 00:01:55,574
He does look sweet.

45
00:01:55,658 --> 00:01:58,285
I think he's sweet when he tries to be.

46
00:02:00,538 --> 00:02:03,457
Is there anything that's on your mind?

47
00:02:05,334 --> 00:02:06,710
Hmm.

48
00:02:07,044 --> 00:02:09,380
I mean, I guess,

49
00:02:11,298 --> 00:02:12,800
how do I put it?

50
00:02:13,425 --> 00:02:16,053
Back when we were dating.

51
00:02:16,345 --> 00:02:18,097
You and me?

52
00:02:19,306 --> 00:02:21,141
I thought

53
00:02:21,475 --> 00:02:23,978
I wasn't bothered by it at all,

54
00:02:24,812 --> 00:02:27,231
but I may still have some scars from that.

55
00:02:28,274 --> 00:02:30,651
We're talking over 20 years ago.

56
00:02:31,694 --> 00:02:33,696
And I'm still feeling the pain.

57
00:02:34,738 --> 00:02:37,449
It's something I hadn't even noticed
in myself before.

58
00:02:38,325 --> 00:02:39,410
Yeah.

59
00:02:40,119 --> 00:02:42,371
Apparently, it was painful for me.

60
00:02:43,831 --> 00:02:46,750
Was it the most painful relationship
you've ever had?

61
00:02:47,877 --> 00:02:49,753
Yeah, this feeling…

62
00:02:49,837 --> 00:02:50,671
The first time?

63
00:02:50,754 --> 00:02:51,839
It was only that time.

64
00:02:54,133 --> 00:02:56,760
But Misato-chan is so kind.

65
00:02:56,844 --> 00:02:58,178
She is.

66
00:02:58,512 --> 00:03:01,390
But after you dated me,

67
00:03:01,515 --> 00:03:04,059
you dated other people, right?

68
00:03:05,227 --> 00:03:08,147
How did those go?

69
00:03:09,315 --> 00:03:11,817
Well,

70
00:03:11,901 --> 00:03:13,319
honestly,

71
00:03:13,986 --> 00:03:16,906
I was really

72
00:03:16,989 --> 00:03:20,409
cold to her.

73
00:03:20,576 --> 00:03:22,328
I was like super dry.

74
00:03:23,287 --> 00:03:25,539
I guess it's not right to just
summarize it as dry.

75
00:03:26,165 --> 00:03:28,000
I don't even hold hands.

76
00:03:30,169 --> 00:03:33,923
I might have been viewed as cold.

77
00:03:34,006 --> 00:03:36,133
I think she did.

78
00:03:36,216 --> 00:03:40,179
You know, in the 20-odd years
since we broke up,

79
00:03:41,388 --> 00:03:45,017
I think I fundamentally hadn't changed.

80
00:03:46,352 --> 00:03:49,063
How did that happen?

81
00:03:49,605 --> 00:03:50,689
I mean, you're a good guy.

82
00:03:50,773 --> 00:03:53,984
Misato-chan is so sweet.

83
00:03:54,068 --> 00:03:58,447
When people start dating you,
they think you're super fun.

84
00:03:59,114 --> 00:04:02,117
But once you start dating,
why do you change so suddenly?

85
00:04:02,201 --> 00:04:03,911
I mean,

86
00:04:04,995 --> 00:04:07,289
before we got together, I was the pursuer.

87
00:04:07,373 --> 00:04:08,374
Right.

88
00:04:08,457 --> 00:04:10,417
And then

89
00:04:10,501 --> 00:04:12,294
the situation

90
00:04:12,544 --> 00:04:15,923
kind of feels reversed.

91
00:04:21,261 --> 00:04:24,682
Things would start to bother me,

92
00:04:24,765 --> 00:04:26,976
and I would also

93
00:04:27,059 --> 00:04:29,895
start to see flaws.

94
00:04:29,979 --> 00:04:33,232
Like shoes that aren't neatly aligned,

95
00:04:33,315 --> 00:04:36,110
or not folding
the futon mattress properly.

96
00:04:36,193 --> 00:04:37,653
Or being late.

97
00:04:38,904 --> 00:04:42,574
The perfect ideal version I created
inside my head

98
00:04:42,658 --> 00:04:45,494
starts eroding piece by piece.

99
00:04:47,162 --> 00:04:50,791
I get the sense that you were
trying to be careful,

100
00:04:51,709 --> 00:04:55,087
doing your best not to upset me.

101
00:04:55,170 --> 00:04:56,964
Right?

102
00:04:57,631 --> 00:04:58,841
And

103
00:04:58,924 --> 00:05:00,426
that had become a habit

104
00:05:00,509 --> 00:05:03,220
before we even realized.

105
00:05:05,723 --> 00:05:08,225
That's what it felt like,

106
00:05:08,308 --> 00:05:09,977
now that I look back at it.

107
00:05:13,272 --> 00:05:14,690
Yes,

108
00:05:14,982 --> 00:05:17,693
I was trying my best not to upset you,

109
00:05:18,318 --> 00:05:20,487
and I let you get away with so much.

110
00:05:20,738 --> 00:05:23,115
Even when you just said
"magazine and beer."

111
00:05:23,741 --> 00:05:27,161
But I still didn't break up with you
because I liked you.

112
00:05:27,244 --> 00:05:28,787
While we didn't break up,

113
00:05:30,706 --> 00:05:32,166
I kept thinking,

114
00:05:32,249 --> 00:05:35,169
"Does he really like me?"

115
00:05:39,298 --> 00:05:41,967
Seriously,

116
00:05:44,219 --> 00:05:46,096
that time was truly painful.

117
00:05:48,265 --> 00:05:49,433
I bet.

118
00:05:50,684 --> 00:05:52,686
Having that all come up

119
00:05:53,103 --> 00:05:55,814
twenty-odd years after the fact

120
00:05:55,898 --> 00:05:58,025
must mean it was significant.

121
00:05:59,318 --> 00:06:01,028
I think there was a part of me

122
00:06:01,779 --> 00:06:05,532
that was burying all that
so I didn't remember.

123
00:06:08,202 --> 00:06:10,662
And you know, like yesterday,

124
00:06:10,996 --> 00:06:12,456
or this afternoon when you

125
00:06:13,916 --> 00:06:16,126
were recounting how you
confessed your love

126
00:06:16,210 --> 00:06:17,920
to the others.

127
00:06:18,337 --> 00:06:20,839
Hearing that was really painful, too.

128
00:06:21,840 --> 00:06:26,053
I'm not saying I disliked

129
00:06:26,136 --> 00:06:28,263
your love confession,

130
00:06:29,765 --> 00:06:34,144
but it's like I was the only one
who went through all this pain.

131
00:06:34,812 --> 00:06:35,938
Yeah.

132
00:06:46,448 --> 00:06:49,618
FEBRUARY 11, 2004

133
00:07:07,427 --> 00:07:11,557
But it looks like you're trying to change.

134
00:07:12,057 --> 00:07:16,228
You said that you would change.

135
00:07:21,191 --> 00:07:22,943
I want to make an announcement.

136
00:07:23,652 --> 00:07:24,736
I will change.

137
00:07:24,820 --> 00:07:27,281
I used to be

138
00:07:27,364 --> 00:07:28,991
an incredibly cold person.

139
00:07:29,533 --> 00:07:35,038
I would like to learn more empathy,

140
00:07:35,831 --> 00:07:38,876
and become a person

141
00:07:38,959 --> 00:07:43,922
who is able to be there for my partner.

142
00:07:44,464 --> 00:07:47,593
However, I'm dense, so I might be doing it
without realizing.

143
00:07:47,676 --> 00:07:51,180
So if you could call me out on it,
I'd appreciate it.

144
00:07:53,891 --> 00:07:56,768
This is my determination.

145
00:08:00,981 --> 00:08:05,152
Maybe that's not something
you should be announcing to everyone.

146
00:08:06,361 --> 00:08:09,448
That pissed me off, too.

147
00:08:10,490 --> 00:08:12,034
Like

148
00:08:12,117 --> 00:08:14,703
does he actually want to do that?

149
00:08:18,498 --> 00:08:20,000
You know.

150
00:08:22,628 --> 00:08:25,088
Part of it

151
00:08:26,632 --> 00:08:31,178
is that I wish you had said that
only to me.

152
00:08:31,261 --> 00:08:33,388
Exactly!

153
00:08:33,722 --> 00:08:35,557
Preach!

154
00:08:42,314 --> 00:08:45,609
But that's your personality.

155
00:08:45,692 --> 00:08:49,613
I get why you would announce it like that.

156
00:08:51,990 --> 00:08:53,575
Well said, Misato.

157
00:08:53,659 --> 00:08:54,993
For real.

158
00:08:56,745 --> 00:09:01,500
I had no idea she felt like that.

159
00:09:02,668 --> 00:09:07,506
And I realized

160
00:09:07,589 --> 00:09:10,509
that it must have been
pretty painful for her.

161
00:09:15,264 --> 00:09:18,767
So I invited you here tonight.

162
00:09:18,850 --> 00:09:19,851
Yeah.

163
00:09:22,854 --> 00:09:24,982
I did some awful things to you

164
00:09:27,317 --> 00:09:28,944
even though I cared a lot.

165
00:09:31,863 --> 00:09:34,658
I really wanted to apologize.

166
00:09:36,868 --> 00:09:39,788
Does that mean you feel bad about it?

167
00:09:39,871 --> 00:09:42,791
Yeah.

168
00:09:44,293 --> 00:09:47,170
I've always felt bad about it.

169
00:09:54,303 --> 00:09:56,179
I wasn't very talkative.

170
00:09:56,263 --> 00:09:57,389
For real.

171
00:09:57,472 --> 00:09:59,558
And I didn't show any affection.

172
00:09:59,641 --> 00:10:00,976
Like zero.

173
00:10:01,059 --> 00:10:02,936
It was really zero.

174
00:10:03,020 --> 00:10:04,813
What was that?

175
00:10:05,689 --> 00:10:07,941
I couldn't be honest with myself.

176
00:10:08,859 --> 00:10:10,193
You know?

177
00:10:11,111 --> 00:10:15,115
20-odd years have passed,

178
00:10:19,995 --> 00:10:21,496
and this has been something

179
00:10:21,788 --> 00:10:26,209
I've felt bad about the whole time.

180
00:10:30,130 --> 00:10:31,715
So,

181
00:10:32,341 --> 00:10:34,343
I'm really sorry

182
00:10:35,218 --> 00:10:38,305
for the way I was back then.

183
00:10:40,349 --> 00:10:41,892
That's how I feel.

184
00:10:45,312 --> 00:10:48,899
I was super lame.

185
00:10:57,657 --> 00:10:59,117
I wanted to apologize to you.

186
00:11:02,621 --> 00:11:04,206
But I did love you so much.

187
00:11:10,087 --> 00:11:12,130
That could be the first time

188
00:11:14,341 --> 00:11:17,344
I've ever said I'm sorry.

189
00:11:18,845 --> 00:11:20,555
But

190
00:11:20,764 --> 00:11:24,851
I did feel really bad about it.

191
00:11:29,189 --> 00:11:31,608
I don't know if it's too late
for me to grow

192
00:11:31,983 --> 00:11:35,529
after becoming this crotchety old man,

193
00:11:36,530 --> 00:11:39,116
but I do want to show you a good time.

194
00:11:41,410 --> 00:11:43,412
That's good to hear.

195
00:11:45,705 --> 00:11:48,708
I know I need to get it together.

196
00:11:55,424 --> 00:11:57,843
I was glad

197
00:11:58,135 --> 00:12:00,637
that he apologized.

198
00:12:01,763 --> 00:12:07,477
Rather than thinking about a new romance,

199
00:12:08,019 --> 00:12:10,605
I feel like

200
00:12:11,064 --> 00:12:13,316
I've gained a better understanding of X.

201
00:12:16,194 --> 00:12:18,905
How did you feel about that stuff
with Ryo and Misato?

202
00:12:18,989 --> 00:12:19,823
He apologized.

203
00:12:19,906 --> 00:12:22,534
I could tell he was trying to hide
his embarrassment

204
00:12:22,617 --> 00:12:25,162
by his choice of words and stuff.

205
00:12:25,287 --> 00:12:29,166
But I think he realized it,

206
00:12:29,249 --> 00:12:31,168
and we could see Misato's relief.

207
00:12:31,251 --> 00:12:33,044
And I was relieved by that.

208
00:12:33,128 --> 00:12:35,338
Maybe he talks tough
when he's embarrassed.

209
00:12:36,298 --> 00:12:38,842
He might be from the Edo Era.

210
00:12:39,968 --> 00:12:42,804
Anne, can we believe Ryo when he said

211
00:12:42,888 --> 00:12:44,181
he would change?

212
00:12:46,391 --> 00:12:47,434
What?

213
00:12:47,976 --> 00:12:50,061
You just completely froze.

214
00:12:50,145 --> 00:12:53,482
I do want to respect the feeling
he had at the time.

215
00:12:53,565 --> 00:12:55,775
So I do want to believe him.

216
00:12:55,859 --> 00:12:57,486
Yes, we would like to believe him.

217
00:12:57,569 --> 00:13:00,113
But Ryo-san is also interested in Mao-san.

218
00:13:00,197 --> 00:13:01,031
That's right.

219
00:13:01,114 --> 00:13:02,073
So that's…

220
00:13:02,157 --> 00:13:02,991
That's right!

221
00:13:03,074 --> 00:13:05,452
Things are getting a little complicated.

222
00:13:10,373 --> 00:13:12,167
Wow, that's cold.

223
00:13:12,626 --> 00:13:15,045
You okay? Sorry, it'll just be a second.

224
00:13:16,379 --> 00:13:19,257
I think it's Hiroyoshi-san and Yoko-san.

225
00:13:21,968 --> 00:13:23,220
Let's go on a date tomorrow.

226
00:13:25,430 --> 00:13:28,767
We'll meet at 9:45 tomorrow
in front of the elevator.

227
00:13:28,850 --> 00:13:30,936
What are we going to do?

228
00:13:31,019 --> 00:13:32,562
You want me to tell you?

229
00:13:32,646 --> 00:13:33,730
Yes.

230
00:13:34,314 --> 00:13:36,525
Hold on, can I think on it?

231
00:13:36,942 --> 00:13:38,652
Whether or not to go.

232
00:13:39,069 --> 00:13:40,278
I see.

233
00:13:40,362 --> 00:13:41,488
Right.

234
00:13:41,571 --> 00:13:44,241
Yoko-san has the guts to say no
when she needs to.

235
00:13:44,699 --> 00:13:45,951
I'll go.

236
00:13:46,034 --> 00:13:49,079
Thank goodness. If you said no,
I don't think I'd recover.

237
00:13:49,162 --> 00:13:51,498
I'll go.

238
00:13:51,706 --> 00:13:53,041
Thank goodness.

239
00:13:53,166 --> 00:13:55,669
That time you needed to think scared me.

240
00:13:56,086 --> 00:13:58,964
But if I'm not there at 9:45 tomorrow,

241
00:13:59,047 --> 00:14:00,507
you should take that as me not going.

242
00:14:00,590 --> 00:14:02,259
So that's a possibility.

243
00:14:02,342 --> 00:14:04,177
Fair enough.

244
00:14:04,261 --> 00:14:06,846
That kind of attitude is not good.

245
00:14:06,930 --> 00:14:08,598
Of course I want to go.

246
00:14:09,307 --> 00:14:11,810
But right, I shouldn't be acting
like such a defeatist.

247
00:14:12,227 --> 00:14:13,812
I want to go with you a whole lot.

248
00:14:13,895 --> 00:14:16,356
Then I'll…

249
00:14:20,235 --> 00:14:21,403
That's long.

250
00:14:22,404 --> 00:14:23,280
Will go!

251
00:14:23,363 --> 00:14:24,197
Thank you.

252
00:14:24,281 --> 00:14:26,241
Hiroyoshi-san seems to let her
get away with it.

253
00:14:26,324 --> 00:14:27,701
He's like, "Why, you little…!"

254
00:14:27,784 --> 00:14:32,622
Hiroyoshi-san thinks Yoko-san
is sweet on him.

255
00:14:33,373 --> 00:14:35,125
In the end, I still think

256
00:14:35,208 --> 00:14:38,211
I need to face my X.

257
00:14:38,295 --> 00:14:40,964
We haven't resolved our past yet.

258
00:14:41,172 --> 00:14:42,674
My new goal is to

259
00:14:42,757 --> 00:14:45,385
clearly tell him

260
00:14:45,468 --> 00:14:48,013
exactly what my issues were with him.

261
00:14:48,096 --> 00:14:49,806
And I need to hear how he feels.

262
00:14:49,889 --> 00:14:52,309
Sounds like she wants to point out
things she disliked from the past.

263
00:14:52,892 --> 00:14:55,312
This is my first time cutting
a green pepper.

264
00:14:56,271 --> 00:14:57,188
So we take out the seeds.

265
00:14:57,272 --> 00:14:59,983
Good job. We learn as we do.

266
00:15:00,066 --> 00:15:03,486
Please be gentle as I am a total beginner.

267
00:15:04,237 --> 00:15:07,532
Looks like he's trying to overcome
his trauma.

268
00:15:08,074 --> 00:15:10,493
Right, because learning how to cook
is the fastest way

269
00:15:10,577 --> 00:15:12,662
in Hiroyoshi-san's case.

270
00:15:14,039 --> 00:15:16,291
Wow, I want to just eat this now.

271
00:15:16,374 --> 00:15:17,500
True.

272
00:15:17,584 --> 00:15:18,793
It looks so good.

273
00:15:20,420 --> 00:15:21,546
Just a nibble.

274
00:15:21,630 --> 00:15:23,882
It's so good on its own.

275
00:15:26,343 --> 00:15:27,469
Wow.

276
00:15:27,552 --> 00:15:28,637
It's pizza.

277
00:15:29,638 --> 00:15:31,097
So I guess

278
00:15:31,181 --> 00:15:33,350
we do this in the air.

279
00:15:34,976 --> 00:15:36,102
That's so pretty.

280
00:15:36,186 --> 00:15:37,020
Nice work.

281
00:15:37,103 --> 00:15:39,064
I'm so excited for this.

282
00:15:39,147 --> 00:15:40,565
It's going to be good for sure.

283
00:15:40,649 --> 00:15:42,525
I'm pretty hungry.

284
00:15:42,692 --> 00:15:44,277
Raise it up like this?

285
00:15:44,486 --> 00:15:47,113
You're looking pretty shaky.

286
00:15:48,865 --> 00:15:52,410
Yoko-san slips into the Kansai dialect
when it's just the two of them.

287
00:15:52,869 --> 00:15:54,621
That looks delicious.

288
00:15:54,704 --> 00:15:56,373
I'm hungry.

289
00:15:58,667 --> 00:15:59,668
Kanako, good morning.

290
00:15:59,751 --> 00:16:00,835
Good morning.

291
00:16:05,340 --> 00:16:08,259
Poor Kanako-chan.

292
00:16:11,805 --> 00:16:13,682
Sorry to bring you out here
when I'm dressed like this.

293
00:16:14,557 --> 00:16:16,601
It's fine. You look cute. What's up?

294
00:16:17,310 --> 00:16:18,478
Sorry about the other day.

295
00:16:18,561 --> 00:16:19,521
Don't mention it.

296
00:16:20,063 --> 00:16:21,815
I'm done for today.

297
00:16:22,857 --> 00:16:24,359
What do you mean?

298
00:16:24,734 --> 00:16:26,486
I'm going back.

299
00:16:26,820 --> 00:16:29,030
She got too annoyed with Satoshi.

300
00:16:29,114 --> 00:16:31,866
She kind of ruined the vibes at the time.

301
00:16:31,950 --> 00:16:34,202
You know how we talked about
holding things in,

302
00:16:34,285 --> 00:16:38,331
and how to vent our stress?

303
00:16:38,415 --> 00:16:41,042
But I just couldn't in that situation.

304
00:16:41,126 --> 00:16:41,960
It's fine.

305
00:16:42,043 --> 00:16:45,672
You could say that aligned perfectly
with who you are.

306
00:16:45,755 --> 00:16:48,591
I don't think you need to

307
00:16:48,675 --> 00:16:50,760
worry about everyone individually.

308
00:16:50,844 --> 00:16:53,388
I think we should all just follow our
feelings and act on them.

309
00:16:53,471 --> 00:16:56,057
I also think Satoshi

310
00:16:56,141 --> 00:16:57,767
has his own ideas.

311
00:16:57,851 --> 00:17:00,270
However you feel

312
00:17:00,353 --> 00:17:05,024
about Satoshi right now,

313
00:17:06,901 --> 00:17:08,820
those are your feelings.

314
00:17:08,903 --> 00:17:12,449
But Satoshi isn't obligated

315
00:17:13,908 --> 00:17:16,494
to reciprocate those feelings

316
00:17:16,578 --> 00:17:18,204
in this hocance.

317
00:17:21,124 --> 00:17:22,917
But Satoshi looks down.

318
00:17:24,544 --> 00:17:27,714
I've already given up.

319
00:17:27,797 --> 00:17:30,008
I'm not looking at X anymore.

320
00:17:30,091 --> 00:17:32,427
So Kanako's moved on from Satoshi?

321
00:17:32,510 --> 00:17:34,971
She just said she's given up.

322
00:17:35,054 --> 00:17:36,473
Look, don't jump the gun yet.

323
00:17:36,556 --> 00:17:39,017
We still have the vacation to come.

324
00:17:39,184 --> 00:17:43,313
All you have to do is act on your
feelings like you have.

325
00:17:43,396 --> 00:17:44,606
Thanks.

326
00:17:44,689 --> 00:17:46,065
Thanks for talking to me.

327
00:17:46,149 --> 00:17:48,026
She's asking him for advice.

328
00:17:48,109 --> 00:17:49,194
Yes.

329
00:17:50,820 --> 00:17:51,696
Wow.

330
00:17:51,780 --> 00:17:52,614
Okay.

331
00:17:53,031 --> 00:17:54,908
Let's dig in.

332
00:17:54,991 --> 00:17:56,159
I'm hungry.

333
00:17:57,076 --> 00:17:58,244
Yum.

334
00:17:59,120 --> 00:18:00,622
Is it good?

335
00:18:01,748 --> 00:18:03,333
This dough is good.

336
00:18:05,460 --> 00:18:06,294
It really is.

337
00:18:06,377 --> 00:18:07,337
Perfect score.

338
00:18:09,047 --> 00:18:10,298
That's good.

339
00:18:10,381 --> 00:18:13,092
I've never gone on a date like this.

340
00:18:16,221 --> 00:18:19,265
It feels really fresh.

341
00:18:19,349 --> 00:18:20,183
Yeah.

342
00:18:21,893 --> 00:18:23,311
You know, yesterday,

343
00:18:23,394 --> 00:18:26,981
Satoshi, Kanako, Misato, and I

344
00:18:27,065 --> 00:18:28,900
were talking about marriage.

345
00:18:29,359 --> 00:18:31,319
When I asked Satoshi

346
00:18:32,403 --> 00:18:34,489
if he wanted to get married, he said yes.

347
00:18:34,572 --> 00:18:35,990
Yeah?

348
00:18:36,074 --> 00:18:38,910
He wants to get married quickly
if he finds someone good.

349
00:18:39,744 --> 00:18:41,120
You know.

350
00:18:42,038 --> 00:18:45,208
He has a very positive image of marriage.

351
00:18:45,291 --> 00:18:46,835
That's wonderful.

352
00:18:47,335 --> 00:18:50,672
But every man gets married
with that belief.

353
00:18:50,755 --> 00:18:53,091
We just ended up like this because
that didn't happen.

354
00:18:53,174 --> 00:18:55,677
So I made sure I let him know that, too.

355
00:18:55,760 --> 00:18:58,555
Was that really necessary to mention
to burst his bubble?

356
00:18:59,055 --> 00:19:00,807
And anyone else's?

357
00:19:01,599 --> 00:19:03,560
I'm not sure.

358
00:19:03,643 --> 00:19:05,311
I wonder.

359
00:19:06,062 --> 00:19:08,982
I didn't think there was anyone

360
00:19:09,065 --> 00:19:10,942
who had given up on marriage already.

361
00:19:11,025 --> 00:19:12,694
Do you want to get married?

362
00:19:12,777 --> 00:19:14,904
I told him that I didn't at this moment.

363
00:19:17,073 --> 00:19:18,116
Why not?

364
00:19:18,741 --> 00:19:22,370
Part of it is that I already failed
at it once.

365
00:19:22,453 --> 00:19:24,956
If my partner wants to get married
and have kids,

366
00:19:25,039 --> 00:19:27,458
then I will understand.

367
00:19:27,792 --> 00:19:29,794
If not,

368
00:19:29,878 --> 00:19:33,673
then I think just being a good partner
for the foreseeable future is good enough.

369
00:19:33,756 --> 00:19:37,510
I told him

370
00:19:37,594 --> 00:19:39,804
that in my opinion,

371
00:19:39,888 --> 00:19:42,181
marriage wasn't strictly necessary.

372
00:19:44,601 --> 00:19:48,146
I explained that it all depends
on the situation.

373
00:19:49,063 --> 00:19:50,565
Situation?

374
00:19:52,025 --> 00:19:53,192
She's pressing him.

375
00:19:53,276 --> 00:19:54,569
She's a CEO after all.

376
00:19:54,652 --> 00:19:59,616
I just let him know that I'm not
thinking of marriage right now.

377
00:20:02,452 --> 00:20:03,286
Are you, Yoko-chan?

378
00:20:03,369 --> 00:20:04,203
Not at all.

379
00:20:04,287 --> 00:20:05,288
I didn't think so.

380
00:20:05,371 --> 00:20:06,956
What do you mean by that?

381
00:20:07,040 --> 00:20:08,124
Because I knew you weren't.

382
00:20:08,207 --> 00:20:09,125
Yikes.

383
00:20:09,208 --> 00:20:11,210
But I might consider it if I had someone.

384
00:20:11,294 --> 00:20:13,338
It depends on the man.

385
00:20:13,421 --> 00:20:15,590
If I feel deep down
that I want to marry him.

386
00:20:15,673 --> 00:20:16,591
I see.

387
00:20:16,674 --> 00:20:18,760
It's not like I've decided never
to get married.

388
00:20:18,843 --> 00:20:19,928
Oh, yeah?

389
00:20:20,053 --> 00:20:20,887
So it depends.

390
00:20:20,970 --> 00:20:22,013
I can't say definitively.

391
00:20:22,096 --> 00:20:23,681
Could you pass me a wipe?

392
00:20:23,765 --> 00:20:25,141
A wet wipe.

393
00:20:25,600 --> 00:20:29,646
Because I believe

394
00:20:29,729 --> 00:20:33,024
that marriage
is the ultimate responsibility.

395
00:20:33,900 --> 00:20:37,278
If you're not interested in that,

396
00:20:38,363 --> 00:20:41,366
that comes off as rude to me.

397
00:20:42,116 --> 00:20:44,869
I don't think I said anything that would
leave such a bad impression.

398
00:20:45,203 --> 00:20:46,621
In my opinion…

399
00:20:46,704 --> 00:20:48,206
This is fun.

400
00:20:48,289 --> 00:20:49,749
They're like a married couple.

401
00:20:49,832 --> 00:20:50,667
Exactly.

402
00:20:50,750 --> 00:20:52,794
There's this tension.

403
00:20:53,419 --> 00:20:55,713
…I don't think everyone feels that way.

404
00:20:55,797 --> 00:20:58,049
You made it sound like
that's what I'm saying,

405
00:20:58,132 --> 00:21:00,468
but I never said anything like that.

406
00:21:00,551 --> 00:21:02,011
This is fun.

407
00:21:02,095 --> 00:21:04,180
He can't look up anymore.

408
00:21:04,263 --> 00:21:07,350
I love the way Hiroyoshi-san
defends himself.

409
00:21:08,893 --> 00:21:11,938
The way I see it,
not wanting to take responsibility

410
00:21:12,021 --> 00:21:15,942
equals not seeking out marriage.

411
00:21:16,025 --> 00:21:17,485
And I despise that.

412
00:21:17,568 --> 00:21:21,239
It reminded me of why
I couldn't be with X anymore.

413
00:21:21,864 --> 00:21:25,493
So I just started spacing out.

414
00:21:25,660 --> 00:21:28,955
Whenever X is bothered by anything,

415
00:21:29,163 --> 00:21:31,207
or gets in a bad mood,

416
00:21:31,290 --> 00:21:33,126
I can't help but turn into Mr. Timid.

417
00:21:33,209 --> 00:21:35,128
Who's Mr. Timid?

418
00:21:37,046 --> 00:21:38,798
So…

419
00:21:38,881 --> 00:21:40,758
wanting to be a housewife
is a dealbreaker?

420
00:21:40,842 --> 00:21:42,176
He's still getting scolded.

421
00:21:42,260 --> 00:21:43,219
Yeah.

422
00:21:43,302 --> 00:21:44,178
Why?

423
00:21:44,846 --> 00:21:47,181
I think I'd prefer

424
00:21:47,265 --> 00:21:49,475
if we both worked a bit

425
00:21:49,559 --> 00:21:51,144
and supported each other.

426
00:21:51,227 --> 00:21:53,187
So you prefer someone who works.

427
00:21:53,271 --> 00:21:55,940
Well, yeah…
especially if we talk about having kids,

428
00:21:56,107 --> 00:21:58,359
there's everything that comes after that.

429
00:21:58,776 --> 00:21:59,902
What do you mean by 'after'?

430
00:21:59,986 --> 00:22:02,363
I mean, my own work
might gradually taper off,

431
00:22:02,447 --> 00:22:04,824
so managing that…

432
00:22:04,907 --> 00:22:07,994
plus raising kids costs
tens of millions of yen.

433
00:22:08,161 --> 00:22:09,954
Interrogation room inside the car.

434
00:22:12,665 --> 00:22:15,376
I think I see things a bit differently.

435
00:22:15,460 --> 00:22:16,711
Oh, really?

436
00:22:17,920 --> 00:22:19,756
I expected you to say something like,

437
00:22:19,839 --> 00:22:24,469
"I think working women are attractive"…

438
00:22:24,552 --> 00:22:25,428
Of course I do.

439
00:22:25,553 --> 00:22:29,932
…but you didn't say that.

440
00:22:30,016 --> 00:22:31,476
You jump straight to conclusions.

441
00:22:31,601 --> 00:22:33,478
It's not a conclusion,
just what I expected.

442
00:22:33,561 --> 00:22:34,395
Right, okay.

443
00:22:34,479 --> 00:22:39,358
Your answer was different from
what I thought you'd say.

444
00:22:39,442 --> 00:22:41,152
Of course there's more than that.

445
00:22:41,235 --> 00:22:42,653
I mean, I do think you shine

446
00:22:42,737 --> 00:22:43,946
when you're working.

447
00:22:44,030 --> 00:22:46,574
But what if I wanted to become
a full-time housewife?

448
00:22:47,033 --> 00:22:48,326
What would you do?

449
00:22:48,409 --> 00:22:49,452
I see.

450
00:22:49,535 --> 00:22:51,537
Then I'd cross that bridge
when we get there.

451
00:22:52,205 --> 00:22:54,916
Think about it now. Imagine it.

452
00:22:55,124 --> 00:22:56,667
But honestly, if you were like that,

453
00:22:56,751 --> 00:22:57,877
I don't think I'd fall for you.

454
00:22:59,045 --> 00:22:59,879
Why?

455
00:22:59,962 --> 00:23:01,089
Because I was drawn to

456
00:23:01,172 --> 00:23:03,883
your ambition and how hard you work.

457
00:23:04,217 --> 00:23:06,177
If you suddenly quit your job,

458
00:23:06,260 --> 00:23:08,346
stayed home doing nothing,
and were just like,

459
00:23:08,429 --> 00:23:09,305
"I'll try cooking"…

460
00:23:09,388 --> 00:23:10,556
Not "doing nothing."

461
00:23:10,640 --> 00:23:13,851
I meant shifting focus to
taking care of the home.

462
00:23:14,018 --> 00:23:15,144
Of course.

463
00:23:15,269 --> 00:23:17,897
Or something like that.

464
00:23:17,980 --> 00:23:19,065
That's unlikely.

465
00:23:19,148 --> 00:23:20,149
But hypothetically…

466
00:23:20,233 --> 00:23:21,359
No, it won't.

467
00:23:21,442 --> 00:23:22,610
But if it did!

468
00:23:22,693 --> 00:23:24,654
Then, I'd give up.

469
00:23:24,737 --> 00:23:26,614
Give up?

470
00:23:26,697 --> 00:23:28,199
So you'd stop loving me?

471
00:23:28,282 --> 00:23:32,036
No, no, no. It's just…
I wouldn't want to see you like that.

472
00:23:32,203 --> 00:23:34,747
I said I wouldn't even picture that.

473
00:23:35,832 --> 00:23:38,709
But that's a worst-case scenario.

474
00:23:43,297 --> 00:23:47,844
I want a partner who's serious enough

475
00:23:47,927 --> 00:23:50,012
to be thinking about marriage.

476
00:23:50,096 --> 00:23:52,431
Even if we don't actually get married,

477
00:23:53,057 --> 00:23:56,102
I just don't want a guy
saying things like,

478
00:23:56,185 --> 00:23:58,521
"I'm never marrying."

479
00:23:58,938 --> 00:24:03,901
That's actually a super important
standard for me.

480
00:24:04,402 --> 00:24:08,406
Today made me realize,

481
00:24:08,489 --> 00:24:10,366
"Ah, so this is where our values clash."

482
00:24:10,992 --> 00:24:12,243
Once it hit me,

483
00:24:13,536 --> 00:24:15,955
I was like… yeah, this is bad.

484
00:24:16,080 --> 00:24:18,833
Things are looking pretty stormy.

485
00:24:21,002 --> 00:24:22,587
Well, yeah…

486
00:24:22,670 --> 00:24:25,673
I guess you could call it
a productive date.

487
00:24:26,841 --> 00:24:28,009
Wow, total polar opposites.

488
00:24:28,092 --> 00:24:29,510
They're saying the exact opposite.

489
00:24:29,635 --> 00:24:31,095
The gap between men and women is insane.

490
00:24:31,179 --> 00:24:32,513
This is interesting.

491
00:24:32,597 --> 00:24:34,432
Productive date.

492
00:24:34,765 --> 00:24:38,060
That pretty much sums it up.

493
00:24:38,144 --> 00:24:42,607
This was the first date

494
00:24:43,399 --> 00:24:47,820
where I could finally have a real,
face-to-face talk with my ex.

495
00:24:47,904 --> 00:24:50,990
Right from the car,
she was hit with a barrage of questions.

496
00:24:51,073 --> 00:24:54,035
Hearing her

497
00:24:54,410 --> 00:24:57,872
strong responses to my answers

498
00:24:57,955 --> 00:25:00,374
felt pretty fresh to me.

499
00:25:02,585 --> 00:25:04,253
He's pretty blissful.

500
00:25:04,337 --> 00:25:06,672
Talk about positive thinking!

501
00:25:09,884 --> 00:25:12,136
Cute stained glass.

502
00:25:13,888 --> 00:25:15,806
Time really flew by, though.

503
00:25:16,390 --> 00:25:19,101
Is this Daichi and Kaede?

504
00:25:19,852 --> 00:25:23,898
I actually had a reason for
asking you out today.

505
00:25:25,733 --> 00:25:27,193
Like…

506
00:25:27,902 --> 00:25:30,238
me being a wall?

507
00:25:31,239 --> 00:25:32,907
A wall?

508
00:25:32,990 --> 00:25:34,951
Yeah, breaking that down,

509
00:25:35,034 --> 00:25:36,702
and hoping you could

510
00:25:36,786 --> 00:25:39,121
see a changed version of me.

511
00:25:39,205 --> 00:25:40,623
Will I get to see it?

512
00:25:40,706 --> 00:25:41,999
You will.

513
00:25:42,833 --> 00:25:45,127
Did you feel like there was a wall?

514
00:25:45,378 --> 00:25:48,005
Not everywhere,

515
00:25:48,089 --> 00:25:50,841
but I felt it here and there.

516
00:25:52,176 --> 00:25:53,511
I see.

517
00:25:57,139 --> 00:25:59,684
Like, moments where

518
00:25:59,767 --> 00:26:03,771
you wouldn't let me in.

519
00:26:04,939 --> 00:26:06,232
Alright.

520
00:26:06,357 --> 00:26:09,652
Even when we broke up,

521
00:26:10,528 --> 00:26:13,739
I never really knew the real reason,

522
00:26:14,115 --> 00:26:15,574
you know?

523
00:26:15,658 --> 00:26:16,492
I see.

524
00:26:16,575 --> 00:26:17,410
Would she tell him?

525
00:26:19,996 --> 00:26:21,622
Daichi-san…

526
00:26:21,706 --> 00:26:24,709
Whenever he wanted to step closer,

527
00:26:24,792 --> 00:26:27,169
he thought I didn't want him

528
00:26:27,253 --> 00:26:29,714
to come closer to me.

529
00:26:29,797 --> 00:26:31,382
That's why…

530
00:26:31,465 --> 00:26:35,386
he backed off, thinking
he shouldn't push any further.

531
00:26:35,720 --> 00:26:38,514
In past relationships,

532
00:26:38,597 --> 00:26:39,640
guys always

533
00:26:39,724 --> 00:26:42,935
pushed past my boundaries anyway.

534
00:26:43,477 --> 00:26:49,275
But he was gentle and always pulled back.

535
00:26:49,358 --> 00:26:51,861
And because he didn't step in,

536
00:26:51,944 --> 00:26:53,362
I felt that wall.

537
00:26:53,821 --> 00:26:54,905
I see.

538
00:26:54,989 --> 00:26:57,700
So both of them felt a wall between them.

539
00:27:03,039 --> 00:27:04,707
Are you glad we came on this hocance?

540
00:27:09,462 --> 00:27:10,629
What about you?

541
00:27:10,713 --> 00:27:12,006
I'm really glad we did.

542
00:27:12,548 --> 00:27:14,592
I was wondering how you felt.

543
00:27:15,968 --> 00:27:18,471
I wasn't sure where your head was at,

544
00:27:18,888 --> 00:27:20,181
but I wanted to know how you felt.

545
00:27:26,854 --> 00:27:28,606
I…

546
00:27:29,565 --> 00:27:32,193
Do you…

547
00:27:32,485 --> 00:27:35,654
still see me that way?

548
00:27:36,864 --> 00:27:37,823
Do you?

549
00:27:37,907 --> 00:27:39,158
Me?

550
00:27:39,784 --> 00:27:40,993
Yes.

551
00:27:41,577 --> 00:27:43,913
Are you still attracted to me?

552
00:27:45,873 --> 00:27:46,791
Yeah.

553
00:27:51,879 --> 00:27:54,090
I think I get what you're trying to say.

554
00:27:57,843 --> 00:28:00,471
Maybe he felt a bit guilty or hesitant?

555
00:28:05,226 --> 00:28:08,979
You never really crossed that line, right?

556
00:28:10,064 --> 00:28:11,315
So…

557
00:28:11,565 --> 00:28:15,528
I couldn't tell if you were
