been creepy the whole time. Same as ever.

842
00:42:22,999 --> 00:42:24,626
Is he trying to do something?

843
00:42:25,919 --> 00:42:27,545
Well…

844
00:42:28,046 --> 00:42:32,217
he does have genuine feelings…

845
00:42:32,300 --> 00:42:33,551
I don't think so.

846
00:42:36,263 --> 00:42:40,183
Satoshi might actually be
showing his truest self.

847
00:42:40,267 --> 00:42:41,142
Maybe.

848
00:42:41,226 --> 00:42:43,561
Out of everyone on this trip…

849
00:42:43,645 --> 00:42:44,604
If so, I can't stand it.

850
00:42:44,688 --> 00:42:47,983
But I feel like that's totally fine.

851
00:42:48,066 --> 00:42:50,485
Personally, anyway.

852
00:42:50,568 --> 00:42:52,404
I'm devoted to one person, so…

853
00:42:52,487 --> 00:42:54,698
it makes it hard for me
to understand that side of him.

854
00:42:57,659 --> 00:43:00,120
So we know Yoko's X is Hiro.

855
00:43:00,578 --> 00:43:02,038
We got a message!

856
00:43:02,122 --> 00:43:03,415
I thought so.

857
00:43:06,501 --> 00:43:07,502
Apparently.

858
00:43:07,585 --> 00:43:08,753
Dating their exes, huh?

859
00:43:08,837 --> 00:43:10,672
Exes…

860
00:43:10,755 --> 00:43:12,966
They spend a lot of time
with their exes here.

861
00:43:13,049 --> 00:43:14,342
That's true.

862
00:43:15,719 --> 00:43:17,262
An ex-date, huh?

863
00:43:19,097 --> 00:43:20,265
You look like you hate the idea.

864
00:43:20,974 --> 00:43:22,392
Not at all.

865
00:43:23,143 --> 00:43:25,854
It's been forever since it was
just the two of us in Okinawa.

866
00:43:27,397 --> 00:43:28,565
Yeah, that's true.

867
00:43:29,816 --> 00:43:31,276
We used to…

868
00:43:31,359 --> 00:43:35,071
come to Okinawa a lot as a family…

869
00:43:35,155 --> 00:43:38,158
and of course, it's a place

870
00:43:38,241 --> 00:43:40,869
full of memories from
before we got married.

871
00:43:40,952 --> 00:43:41,870
Oh, really?

872
00:43:41,953 --> 00:43:44,789
So being in Okinawa without the kids…

873
00:43:44,956 --> 00:43:47,083
it's probably been like 20 years.

874
00:43:47,167 --> 00:43:51,046
I'd like to enjoy this like

875
00:43:51,129 --> 00:43:54,299
when we first started dating,

876
00:43:54,382 --> 00:43:57,886
while also staying focused and
getting things clear between us.

877
00:43:58,386 --> 00:43:59,554
Yes, stay focused.

878
00:43:59,637 --> 00:44:01,139
Like before a big game.

879
00:44:02,223 --> 00:44:03,683
I'm so happy.

880
00:44:03,767 --> 00:44:05,602
Looking forward to it.

881
00:44:05,935 --> 00:44:07,562
This is basically a honeymoon for them.

882
00:44:07,645 --> 00:44:08,897
Looking forward to it.

883
00:44:11,316 --> 00:44:12,776
Looking forward to it.

884
00:44:15,570 --> 00:44:17,906
Look at Satoshi's face!

885
00:44:18,823 --> 00:44:20,408
Wait, who's my ex again?

886
00:44:20,492 --> 00:44:21,785
Over there!

887
00:44:22,494 --> 00:44:23,620
Hey!

888
00:44:25,288 --> 00:44:27,207
Destroy.

889
00:44:28,041 --> 00:44:28,875
Destroy.

890
00:44:28,958 --> 00:44:30,126
Nice to be with you.

891
00:44:30,210 --> 00:44:31,669
Have fun.

892
00:44:31,753 --> 00:44:33,213
Have fun.

893
00:44:35,298 --> 00:44:37,425
Look a little happier about it!

894
00:44:39,344 --> 00:44:40,178
Come over here.

895
00:44:40,261 --> 00:44:41,137
Satoshi, go on over!

896
00:44:41,221 --> 00:44:42,305
Wait, I'm going over now.

897
00:44:42,680 --> 00:44:43,515
You're going?

898
00:44:43,598 --> 00:44:45,183
Suddenly in Kansai dialect?

899
00:44:45,266 --> 00:44:46,726
Where are you going?

900
00:44:47,852 --> 00:44:49,145
"I'm going over now"?

901
00:44:49,938 --> 00:44:51,439
Oh, me?

902
00:44:54,067 --> 00:44:57,529
But he has a date with Kanako tomorrow.

903
00:44:57,904 --> 00:45:00,031
That's probably why
he feels like this right now.

904
00:45:00,698 --> 00:45:02,700
I am seriously dreading tomorrow.

905
00:45:02,909 --> 00:45:04,536
Of course she feels that way.

906
00:45:05,578 --> 00:45:06,788
Kanako.

907
00:45:07,872 --> 00:45:12,127
You said you were gonna make
all five guys fall for you, right?

908
00:45:12,544 --> 00:45:14,879
There's still Hiro, and Dai…

909
00:45:14,963 --> 00:45:16,047
I can't win over Dai.

910
00:45:16,131 --> 00:45:18,341
Can't win over the older guys.

911
00:45:18,425 --> 00:45:20,176
Older guys are hard.

912
00:45:20,760 --> 00:45:22,011
She said it loud and clear.

913
00:45:22,095 --> 00:45:24,389
She called us "The Silver Squad" earlier.

914
00:45:24,848 --> 00:45:27,142
With four of us here,
it's "The Silver Squad."

915
00:45:28,017 --> 00:45:29,853
I'm the senior one.

916
00:45:30,395 --> 00:45:32,063
Senior Guy.

917
00:45:32,147 --> 00:45:34,858
Come on, Senior Guy, step up!

918
00:45:37,193 --> 00:45:39,028
Do something!

919
00:45:39,320 --> 00:45:40,780
Do what?

920
00:45:41,489 --> 00:45:43,158
She is getting hit on!

921
00:45:43,950 --> 00:45:46,244
Haste makes waste.

922
00:45:47,996 --> 00:45:50,915
He's so old that
he started quoting proverbs!

923
00:45:52,250 --> 00:45:55,086
Classic old-guy move.

924
00:45:55,837 --> 00:45:59,424
It doesn't look like
Hiro is the one initiating, to me.

925
00:45:59,507 --> 00:46:01,843
So I keep thinking,
"Just hit on her already!"

926
00:46:01,926 --> 00:46:03,094
"Go! Go!"

927
00:46:04,345 --> 00:46:05,513
Fair enough.

928
00:46:05,597 --> 00:46:06,931
Go for it now!

929
00:46:07,015 --> 00:46:08,975
Call out, "Hold on a second!"

930
00:46:11,060 --> 00:46:12,812
So you're not curious about Sato-chan?

931
00:46:12,896 --> 00:46:13,730
True.

932
00:46:13,813 --> 00:46:15,899
Honestly, I want Kanako to
stir things up a bit.

933
00:46:17,108 --> 00:46:19,194
But Kanako never actually makes a move!

934
00:46:19,277 --> 00:46:21,488
Hold on.

935
00:46:21,571 --> 00:46:23,448
I have high hopes for Kanako.

936
00:46:24,282 --> 00:46:25,783
Remember what you said?

937
00:46:25,867 --> 00:46:28,119
You said you were gonna change.

938
00:46:29,787 --> 00:46:31,581
Not sure what's happening,

939
00:46:31,664 --> 00:46:33,124
but you should just go over there

940
00:46:33,208 --> 00:46:34,542
and push Satoshi into the pool.

941
00:46:34,626 --> 00:46:36,503
Oh, I love that idea!

942
00:46:36,586 --> 00:46:38,046
Say, "Hey you!"

943
00:46:38,129 --> 00:46:39,297
That'd be hilarious.

944
00:46:39,964 --> 00:46:42,258
It's turning into a team sport now!

945
00:46:44,260 --> 00:46:45,178
Where did they go?

946
00:46:45,261 --> 00:46:47,597
There they are.

947
00:46:48,932 --> 00:46:50,058
Hiro, go over there.

948
00:46:50,141 --> 00:46:51,476
Go over there.

949
00:46:51,559 --> 00:46:53,645
Like, "Hold on a second!" style?

950
00:46:53,728 --> 00:46:56,397
Should I go for it?
Throwing it back to old-school Neruton?

951
00:46:56,481 --> 00:46:57,482
That reference is too old!

952
00:46:58,024 --> 00:47:00,818
Time to drop a Rider Kick!

953
00:47:01,194 --> 00:47:02,445
Really?

954
00:47:04,155 --> 00:47:05,990
Can you really pull this off, Hiro-kun?

955
00:47:06,074 --> 00:47:07,200
I'm not that kinda type, though.

956
00:47:08,576 --> 00:47:10,411
This is getting hilarious.

957
00:47:12,580 --> 00:47:14,749
Is he gonna be okay?
Yoko looks ready to snap at him.

958
00:47:14,999 --> 00:47:16,960
Maybe he actually wants to stir the pot.

959
00:47:17,043 --> 00:47:18,211
True.

960
00:47:18,670 --> 00:47:21,297
Thanks. Nice.

961
00:47:21,714 --> 00:47:22,966
Let's take a photo.

962
00:47:23,049 --> 00:47:24,050
Shall we?

963
00:47:24,133 --> 00:47:25,301
Yeah, let's do it.

964
00:47:26,094 --> 00:47:27,470
So picture-perfect.

965
00:47:27,554 --> 00:47:28,888
Seriously.

966
00:47:28,972 --> 00:47:30,682
You look picture-perfect anywhere.

967
00:47:31,849 --> 00:47:33,059
How does it look?

968
00:47:34,018 --> 00:47:36,771
My heart is actually pounding.

969
00:47:36,854 --> 00:47:38,690
You're so beautiful.

970
00:47:39,482 --> 00:47:41,067
I'll take a lot.

971
00:47:41,150 --> 00:47:42,735
The way he's walking.

972
00:47:43,903 --> 00:47:45,196
Is he okay?

973
00:47:45,405 --> 00:47:46,781
Hey, let me in on this too!

974
00:47:46,864 --> 00:47:47,907
That was so loud!

975
00:47:48,408 --> 00:47:49,867
Just the two of you…

976
00:47:50,994 --> 00:47:52,161
This is crazy.

977
00:47:53,329 --> 00:47:55,832
Hilarious! This is so good!

978
00:47:55,915 --> 00:47:57,375
I won't let anyone take my Yoko away.

979
00:47:57,458 --> 00:47:59,085
Can we talk alone for a while?

980
00:47:59,168 --> 00:48:00,169
No, you can't.

981
00:48:00,837 --> 00:48:01,796
No?

982
00:48:01,879 --> 00:48:03,298
Let the three of us talk.

983
00:48:03,423 --> 00:48:05,258
But we're talking…

984
00:48:06,259 --> 00:48:07,594
He actually went over!

985
00:48:12,098 --> 00:48:13,433
Attaboy, Hiro!

986
00:48:13,683 --> 00:48:14,851
Awesome.

987
00:48:14,934 --> 00:48:15,977
Kanako's awesome, too.

988
00:48:16,060 --> 00:48:17,478
Isn't this a first?

989
00:48:17,562 --> 00:48:19,063
Yoko is actually happy about it.

990
00:48:19,147 --> 00:48:21,107
Because she got to see this side of Hiro?

991
00:48:22,233 --> 00:48:23,693
Whoa, bro.

992
00:48:24,861 --> 00:48:27,697
I knew all along

993
00:48:27,780 --> 00:48:30,533
that you were talking to Sato-chan.

994
00:48:31,200 --> 00:48:34,162
But I have no intention of
backing down either.

995
00:48:34,454 --> 00:48:36,748
Hey, wait a second… this is awkward.

996
00:48:36,831 --> 00:48:38,583
It's totally fine.

997
00:48:38,666 --> 00:48:40,877
She always tells me,

998
00:48:40,960 --> 00:48:42,879
"I'm not popular, I'm not popular."

999
00:48:42,962 --> 00:48:45,298
But Sato-chan is into her,

1000
00:48:45,381 --> 00:48:47,800
and maybe Ryo-chan is too.

1001
00:48:47,884 --> 00:48:50,678
So I was just thinking my ex, Yoko-chan,

1002
00:48:50,762 --> 00:48:54,265
is super popular. And that makes me happy.

1003
00:48:54,557 --> 00:48:55,683
But…

1004
00:48:56,768 --> 00:48:58,853
that doesn't mean
I'm gonna just let her go.

1005
00:48:58,936 --> 00:49:00,647
Still,

1006
00:49:00,730 --> 00:49:04,484
whether Yoko-chan chooses me
or someone else is completely her call.

1007
00:49:04,609 --> 00:49:07,737
But now that I'm here,

1008
00:49:07,820 --> 00:49:09,781
I'm not holding back anymore.

1009
00:49:10,198 --> 00:49:11,824
Because I really love Yoko-chan.

1010
00:49:15,745 --> 00:49:19,582
Up until now, I was being careful to
hide that we were exes,

1011
00:49:19,999 --> 00:49:24,003
trying to keep our history quiet…

1012
00:49:24,087 --> 00:49:26,506
but on this vacation,

1013
00:49:26,589 --> 00:49:29,801
I'm done holding back.
That's why I came here.

1014
00:49:29,884 --> 00:49:32,762
In my head, I'm like,
"Don't you take my Yoko-chan."

1015
00:49:33,638 --> 00:49:36,057
But again, Yoko-chan is the one to decide.

1016
00:49:36,182 --> 00:49:39,602
Still, I really respect
your proactiveness.

1017
00:49:39,686 --> 00:49:41,312
I think it's awesome.

1018
00:49:41,979 --> 00:49:44,565
You haven't dated Kanako,

1019
00:49:44,649 --> 00:49:47,235
so you're free to go all out,
which is fine.

1020
00:49:47,318 --> 00:49:49,779
But Yoko-chan and I have history.

1021
00:49:49,862 --> 00:49:50,905
We do?

1022
00:49:52,073 --> 00:49:53,533
Well, yeah.

1023
00:49:53,825 --> 00:49:56,077
We do, right?

1024
00:49:56,369 --> 00:49:58,371
Sorry if you feel like we don't.

1025
00:49:58,454 --> 00:50:00,081
No, we do.

1026
00:50:00,164 --> 00:50:03,960
I wasn't able to show any of that before,

1027
00:50:04,043 --> 00:50:06,421
but on this trip,
everyone knows we're exes.

1028
00:50:06,504 --> 00:50:09,257
So I'm going all in with no regrets.

1029
00:50:09,340 --> 00:50:12,135
I came here having decided that
if I don't leave here with Yoko-chan,

1030
00:50:12,218 --> 00:50:15,263
I'll never see her again
for the rest of my life.

1031
00:50:15,638 --> 00:50:18,850
I already told her that. So…

1032
00:50:18,933 --> 00:50:22,145
I mean, I like you as a guy.

1033
00:50:22,228 --> 00:50:23,521
You're a great guy.

1034
00:50:25,565 --> 00:50:29,569
But I have no intention of letting her go.
Sorry for interrupting your time together.

1035
00:50:29,652 --> 00:50:31,112
No worries at all.

1036
00:50:31,195 --> 00:50:33,573
I just didn't want her thinking,

1037
00:50:33,656 --> 00:50:37,368
"Oh, even if I move on,
he's not gonna come after me."

1038
00:50:37,452 --> 00:50:40,121
So I had to step in. Sorry.

1039
00:50:40,663 --> 00:50:42,999
I'll head back now.

1040
00:50:43,499 --> 00:50:45,626
I'll leave you two to it.

1041
00:50:46,544 --> 00:50:48,463
We'll talk for a bit and head back.

1042
00:50:48,546 --> 00:50:49,964
Yeah. I just came to say that.

1043
00:50:50,047 --> 00:50:50,882
Thanks.

1044
00:50:50,965 --> 00:50:52,925
What a nice guy.

1045
00:50:53,342 --> 00:50:55,928
Wonder how Yoko-san is feeling about this.

1046
00:50:56,012 --> 00:50:58,431
He really wanted to
get that off his chest.

1047
00:50:58,848 --> 00:51:01,559
Of course I'm not totally at ease,

1048
00:51:01,642 --> 00:51:05,438
and he's completely free
to make his move on Yoko-chan.

1049
00:51:05,772 --> 00:51:07,523
But in the middle of all this,

1050
00:51:08,900 --> 00:51:11,944
Kana-chan and Misato-chan were like,

1051
00:51:12,111 --> 00:51:14,822
"Are you really okay with that?"

1052
00:51:14,947 --> 00:51:16,449
So I just had to step in between them.

1053
00:51:16,532 --> 00:51:18,409
How I really feel…

1054
00:51:19,118 --> 00:51:21,788
I needed to make that clear

1055
00:51:21,871 --> 00:51:24,165
to both Sato-chan and Yoko-chan.

1056
00:51:24,916 --> 00:51:27,752
Otherwise, I knew
I'd end up regretting it.

1057
00:51:28,002 --> 00:51:32,173
On this trip, I decided I'm not

1058
00:51:32,256 --> 00:51:34,133
playing it safe anymore.

1059
00:51:34,383 --> 00:51:36,677
That's why I made my move today.

1060
00:51:36,761 --> 00:51:37,970
I see.

1061
00:51:38,179 --> 00:51:39,764
But wait…

1062
00:51:39,889 --> 00:51:42,183
from your perspective,

1063
00:51:42,266 --> 00:51:43,851
weren't you the one who invited him?

1064
00:51:43,935 --> 00:51:44,769
Yeah.

1065
00:51:44,852 --> 00:51:45,937
Okay.

1066
00:51:46,020 --> 00:51:48,189
Do you have any thoughts on all this?

1067
00:51:48,272 --> 00:51:49,524
Just in general.

1068
00:51:49,649 --> 00:51:54,195
Well, as you can see…

1069
00:51:55,404 --> 00:51:57,448
it's half-hearted.

1070
00:51:58,699 --> 00:52:00,827
Our whole dynamic, I mean.

1071
00:52:00,910 --> 00:52:02,662
Whoa, whoa.

1072
00:52:02,745 --> 00:52:04,580
You see that as half-hearted?

1073
00:52:04,747 --> 00:52:07,166
Like I've said over and over…

1074
00:52:07,500 --> 00:52:10,545
He's the guy who won't let go,
but won't commit either.

1075
00:52:10,753 --> 00:52:11,963
Then you gotta choose me.

1076
00:52:12,922 --> 00:52:14,340
Come on.

1077
00:52:14,715 --> 00:52:16,634
Suddenly channeling
full Kyushu macho energy?

1078
00:52:17,176 --> 00:52:19,470
No, seriously, that's really how it was.

1079
00:52:19,762 --> 00:52:23,808
So I have to give him a clear answer.

1080
00:52:24,767 --> 00:52:27,603
For both of our sakes.
Well, for his sake, mostly.

1081
00:52:27,895 --> 00:52:29,480
I think I was being selfish.

1082
00:52:29,856 --> 00:52:30,857
Yeah, fair point.

1083
00:52:31,899 --> 00:52:35,069
Don't you wonder what on earth
there is to talk about?

1084
00:52:35,403 --> 00:52:36,654
On our ex-date?

1085
00:52:36,737 --> 00:52:37,905
Those two.

1086
00:52:37,989 --> 00:52:38,990
Oh, those two?

1087
00:52:39,073 --> 00:52:40,157
What are they talking about?

1088
00:52:40,241 --> 00:52:41,826
You can't help but wonder!

1089
00:52:41,909 --> 00:52:43,536
Maybe Satoshi's opening up.

1090
00:52:43,619 --> 00:52:46,247
But Yoko probably isn't into
Satoshi anyway.

1091
00:52:48,249 --> 00:52:49,417
Life is unpredictable.

1092
00:52:49,500 --> 00:52:51,752
They say life has three slopes.

1093
00:52:52,003 --> 00:52:56,048
Uphill, downhill,
and "never hill," the unexpected.

1094
00:52:56,299 --> 00:53:00,428
So you just never know. Take it from me,
I'm one year older than you.

1095
00:53:00,511 --> 00:53:03,598
If that's the case, I don't wanna go
tomorrow. I wanna go with Hika-chan.

1096
00:53:03,681 --> 00:53:05,016
Go for it!

1097
00:53:05,266 --> 00:53:07,685
I mean, when I watched the DVD…

1098
00:53:07,768 --> 00:53:09,854
I watched it on the last day.

1099
00:53:12,481 --> 00:53:15,902
My ex seemed 100% all-in on me.

1100
00:53:15,985 --> 00:53:18,070
But I don't see any of that.
Isn't that crazy?

1101
00:53:18,154 --> 00:53:19,155
Seriously?

1102
00:53:19,822 --> 00:53:21,616
That's a total shocker.

1103
00:53:24,702 --> 00:53:25,912
I'm scared.

1104
00:53:29,373 --> 00:53:31,459
I want to…

1105
00:53:32,418 --> 00:53:33,836
get back with my ex.

1106
00:53:34,670 --> 00:53:37,340
100%.

1107
00:53:39,050 --> 00:53:40,051
You've gotta be kidding me!

1108
00:53:40,718 --> 00:53:43,763
Satoshi also mentioned
his feelings shifted a bit

1109
00:53:43,846 --> 00:53:46,891
after seeing Kanako's attitude later on.

1110
00:53:46,974 --> 00:53:48,893
I had so many regrets…

1111
00:53:50,519 --> 00:53:53,814
so coming here, I really wanted to…

1112
00:53:54,231 --> 00:53:56,609
express my feelings to my ex.

1113
00:53:56,692 --> 00:53:59,362
And my goal was

1114
00:54:00,571 --> 00:54:04,200
to hopefully leave together.

1115
00:54:05,618 --> 00:54:08,871
I was like, "Wait, he was 100% all-in?!"

1116
00:54:09,080 --> 00:54:11,207
But honestly, if he's 100%,

1117
00:54:11,290 --> 00:54:13,834
why hasn't he made

1118
00:54:13,918 --> 00:54:15,419
a single move?

1119
00:54:16,128 --> 00:54:17,463
It just makes no sense to me.

1120
00:54:18,464 --> 00:54:22,468
Like, "What are you even doing
on this hocance?"

1121
00:54:23,511 --> 00:54:24,971
I was totally freaked out.

1122
00:54:25,972 --> 00:54:27,765
It turned me off even more.

1123
00:54:27,848 --> 00:54:30,142
I don't see a single millimeter of effort.

1124
00:54:30,601 --> 00:54:31,936
So that's how it was.

1125
00:54:32,019 --> 00:54:34,438
Saying he was 100% all-in
and acting like that? Insane.

1126
00:54:34,814 --> 00:54:35,815
Wow.

1127
00:54:35,898 --> 00:54:37,525
Yeah. Total shocker.

1128
00:54:37,608 --> 00:54:40,444
But even if you say that, you never know.

1129
00:54:40,736 --> 00:54:43,948
I mean, there are still a few days left.

1130
00:54:44,031 --> 00:54:47,493
You say all that now, but…

1131
00:54:47,743 --> 00:54:51,372
with tomorrow's X-date coming up,

1132
00:54:51,914 --> 00:54:56,293
you could easily be like,
"Oh, Kanako is pretty great after all."

1133
00:54:56,961 --> 00:54:58,754
Right?

1134
00:54:59,630 --> 00:55:00,881
You don't think that's possible?

1135
00:55:01,090 --> 00:55:02,133
Nah, no way.

1136
00:55:02,216 --> 00:55:03,342
Oh, really?

1137
00:55:03,968 --> 00:55:05,469
But you still never know.

1138
00:55:05,845 --> 00:55:07,847
How are you feeling about the X-date?

1139
00:55:07,930 --> 00:55:08,848
Such a drag.

1140
00:55:08,931 --> 00:55:10,057
Wait a minute…

1141
00:55:10,141 --> 00:55:11,267
That's not good.

1142
00:55:11,350 --> 00:55:12,601
Not looking good.

1143
00:55:14,020 --> 00:55:16,814
Hey, that's mean! So mean.

1144
00:55:16,897 --> 00:55:18,190
Well, it can't be helped.

1145
00:55:19,066 --> 00:55:21,318
I came here to get back together.

1146
00:55:21,402 --> 00:55:24,405
That's for sure.

1147
00:55:25,156 --> 00:55:26,282
But…

1148
00:55:27,783 --> 00:55:29,744
Living together in a group environment

1149
00:55:29,827 --> 00:55:32,538
made me notice things that

1150
00:55:35,207 --> 00:55:36,917
made me think, "this feels off."

1151
00:55:37,001 --> 00:55:37,877
What felt off?

1152
00:55:37,960 --> 00:55:39,128
That was the big turning point?

1153
00:55:42,840 --> 00:55:46,135
She would say the exact opposite of
what I was thinking.

1154
00:55:46,594 --> 00:55:47,636
Huh.

1155
00:55:47,720 --> 00:55:48,846
So hearing

1156
00:55:48,929 --> 00:55:52,516
"Behind those words, I felt this way"

1157
00:55:52,600 --> 00:55:55,394
didn't even matter to me anymore.

1158
00:55:55,603 --> 00:55:58,647
What shocked me was
how different her energy output was.

1159
00:55:59,648 --> 00:56:01,859
That's what I told her.

1160
00:56:02,234 --> 00:56:04,445
And she said,

1161
00:56:04,904 --> 00:56:09,492
"It can't be helped.
This is just who I am."

1162
00:56:10,076 --> 00:56:12,745
So the core values are
just fundamentally different.

1163
00:56:13,162 --> 00:56:17,083
That's because
we didn't date for very long.

1164
00:56:17,166 --> 00:56:18,250
Were you guys even dating?

1165
00:56:22,379 --> 00:56:24,381
I thought we were,

1166
00:56:24,465 --> 00:56:26,550
but if she says we weren't,

1167
00:56:26,634 --> 00:56:29,011
then fine, we weren't.

1168
00:56:29,595 --> 00:56:32,973
If that's what she says,
I'm over it at this point.

1169
00:56:33,057 --> 00:56:34,809
You're more mature than I thought,

1170
00:56:35,142 --> 00:56:36,602
Satoshi.

1171
00:56:37,019 --> 00:56:38,562
I think that's lovely.

1172
00:56:38,646 --> 00:56:41,774
That's not what I'm trying to say.

1173
00:56:41,857 --> 00:56:43,275
What are you trying to say, then?

1174
00:56:44,193 --> 00:56:46,153
I'm trying to say I'm into you!

1175
00:56:48,405 --> 00:56:49,240
Really?

1176
00:56:49,365 --> 00:56:50,199
Oh, boy…

1177
00:56:51,200 --> 00:56:52,034
Don't act like that!

1178
00:56:52,118 --> 00:56:53,119
Don't make me say it!

1179
00:56:53,202 --> 00:56:54,495
Don't act like it's a drag!

1180
00:56:55,162 --> 00:56:56,997
I just can't help thinking he's cute.

1181
00:56:57,915 --> 00:56:59,875
Someone coming at me

1182
00:57:00,960 --> 00:57:03,504
so directly like that…

1183
00:57:04,255 --> 00:57:06,715
is so refreshing.

1184
00:57:06,799 --> 00:57:09,301
It's been way too long.

1185
00:57:09,677 --> 00:57:12,555
I almost feel like I'm the one

1186
00:57:12,638 --> 00:57:14,890
being played a bit.

1187
00:57:15,474 --> 00:57:17,143
That's how it feels.

1188
00:57:17,226 --> 00:57:20,229
I'm kind of captivated.

1189
00:57:20,980 --> 00:57:22,606
Totally distracted by him.

1190
00:57:22,690 --> 00:57:24,066
So things are going well.

1191
00:57:24,150 --> 00:57:25,609
She seems to be having fun.

1192
00:57:25,693 --> 00:57:26,694
She's shaken up.

1193
00:57:26,777 --> 00:57:29,655
Guess it's a kind of thrill
she doesn't usually get.

1194
00:57:31,282 --> 00:57:33,909
Thanks.

1195
00:57:36,537 --> 00:57:37,538
Want me to give you a hug?

1196
00:57:37,705 --> 00:57:39,373
Pass.

1197
00:57:39,748 --> 00:57:40,958
You don't mean it anyway.

1198
00:57:41,709 --> 00:57:42,710
I totally mean it.

1199
00:57:45,045 --> 00:57:46,213
Cute.

1200
00:57:47,298 --> 00:57:48,465
So cute.

1201
00:57:48,549 --> 00:57:50,176
Satoshi is just so cute.

1202
00:57:52,178 --> 00:57:53,470
Wanna come over here?

1203
00:57:53,804 --> 00:57:55,055
Might as well!

1204
00:57:55,181 --> 00:57:56,098
Come here, come on.

1205
00:57:56,182 --> 00:57:57,308
Hold on, ma'am…

1206
00:57:58,517 --> 00:58:00,144
Ah, you smell so good.

1207
00:58:00,227 --> 00:58:01,187
No, you do.

1208
00:58:01,270 --> 00:58:02,438
You always smell amazing.

1209
00:58:02,980 --> 00:58:04,315
Smells so good.

1210
00:58:04,690 --> 00:58:06,400
But you haven't been drinking at all.

1211
00:58:06,483 --> 00:58:08,068
What if everyone's watching us?

1212
00:58:09,236 --> 00:58:10,487
Should I give you a hug?

1213
00:58:12,489 --> 00:58:13,866
A hug…

1214
00:58:13,949 --> 00:58:15,701
A hug is…

1215
00:58:16,994 --> 00:58:18,287
You're so cute.

1216
00:58:27,087 --> 00:58:28,547
Look, the thing is…

1217
00:58:28,631 --> 00:58:31,300
there's something I wanna tell you, Yoko.

1218
00:58:31,383 --> 00:58:32,426
Tell me.

1219
00:58:34,720 --> 00:58:38,766
Actually, there's something
I can only say to you.

1220
00:58:40,017 --> 00:58:41,060
I love you.

1221
00:58:43,062 --> 00:58:44,271
It hurts.

1222
00:58:53,072 --> 00:58:54,907
They're gonna be so mad at us.

1223
00:58:54,990 --> 00:58:58,035
Everyone's gonna be mad.

1224
00:59:02,373 --> 00:59:04,124
This is way too good!

1225
00:59:04,208 --> 00:59:05,668
This is getting crazy.

1226
00:59:11,173 --> 00:59:12,383
She's so close.

1227
00:59:14,051 --> 00:59:15,344
Whoa, hold on!

1228
00:59:15,678 --> 00:59:17,763
Crazy, crazy!

1229
00:59:20,474 --> 00:59:21,350
She's doing it.

1230
00:59:22,184 --> 00:59:23,143
What's this?

1231
00:59:23,227 --> 00:59:24,061
She's gonna push him in.

1232
00:59:24,937 --> 00:59:26,897
Suddenly it feels like a K-drama.

1233
00:59:28,148 --> 00:59:29,858
Wait, what is it? What's going on?
